{
  "module": "Position: where tokens are in the sequence",
  "lesson": {
    "slug": "position-need",
    "title": "Why a transformer needs position information",
    "summary": "Word order carries meaning, but attention on its own cannot see it: reordering the tokens just reorders the outputs. So position has to be supplied explicitly.",
    "covers": ["position-need"],
    "prerequisites": [
      {
        "lesson": "attention-output",
        "reason": "The argument rests on the attention output being a weighted average of values."
      }
    ]
  },
  "screens": [
    {
      "ref": "order-matters",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The dog bit the man",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": " and "
            },
            {
              "text": "The man bit the dog",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": " use exactly the same words. They mean very different things, and the only difference is the "
            },
            {
              "text": "order",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Any model of language has to be able to tell these apart. It has to know "
            },
            {
              "text": "where",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " each token is."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 45)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "embedding-no-place",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "So far, nothing tells the model where a token sits. The embedding lookup gives a token the "
            },
            {
              "text": "same vector wherever it appears",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ". "
            },
            {
              "text": "dog",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": " at the start of a text and "
            },
            {
              "text": "dog",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": " at the end start out identical."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Attention could in principle add the missing information, so the next question is whether it does."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 45, 6)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "attention-blind",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "It does not. Each position's attention output is a weighted average of value vectors, and the weights come from comparing queries with keys. "
            },
            {
              "text": "None of that depends on where a token is in the list.",
              "bold": true
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The result is called "
            },
            {
              "text": "permutation equivariance",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ": reorder the input tokens, and the outputs are the same vectors, reordered in the same way. To attention, the input is a set, not a sequence."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "note",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "This holds for attention as described so far, with nothing to stop a position looking at later tokens."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 45)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "toy-swap",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "A toy check with three tokens whose vectors are (1, 0), (0, 1), (1, 1), using each vector as its own query, key and value."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "text": "In the order 1, 2, 3 the outputs are (0.845, 0.578), (0.578, 0.845), (0.788, 0.788)."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "Now reverse the tokens to 3, 2, 1. The outputs are (0.788, 0.788), (0.578, 0.845), (0.845, 0.578)."
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "They are the same three vectors, in the reverse order. Each token got exactly the same output as before. Attention cannot tell that the order changed."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 45)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "the-fix",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The fix is to "
            },
            {
              "text": "supply position explicitly",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ": give the model something that makes a token at one place different from the same token at another place."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "There are three schemes to meet, in the next lessons. Sinusoidal encodings and a learned table of positions are two ways of adding a position vector to the input. Rotary position embedding (RoPE) instead builds position into the scores."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 45, 46, 47, 48)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "nuance",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "One caveat. Some work reports that when attention is stopped from looking ahead, a model can partly work out position for itself. Kazemnejad et al. (2023) found that models with no position encoding at all can work, and on the tasks they tested generalised to longer sequences better than several explicit schemes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Explicit position schemes remain the standard in practice."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 45)"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "questions": [
    {
      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Why does a transformer need explicit position information?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "options": [
        {
          "correct": true,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "Attention treats its input as a set, so word order is invisible unless it is supplied"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "Reordering the tokens just reorders the outputs in the same way."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "Because the vocabulary has no entry for position"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "The issue is what attention can see, not the vocabulary."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "Because tokens are too long to fit in memory"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "Memory is not the reason."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "Because embeddings change every time the text changes"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "An embedding lookup is the same every time."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "teaches": ["order-matters", "attention-blind"],
      "covers": ["position-need"],
      "variants": [
        {
          "prompt": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "Two texts contain the same tokens in a different order. With no position information, what does attention give for a given token in each?"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "options": [
            {
              "correct": true,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "The same output vector in both, only its place in the list moves"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "reason": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "The output does not depend on where the token sits."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "correct": false,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "Completely different vectors, because the order differs"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "reason": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "That would need attention to see the order, which it cannot."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "correct": false,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "Zero vectors, because the order is unknown"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "reason": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "It still computes its weighted average as usual."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "correct": false,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "An error, because the order is unknown"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "reason": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "Nothing fails. The information just is not there."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Without position information, two tokens in the input are swapped. What happens to the attention outputs?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "options": [
        {
          "correct": true,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "They are swapped in the same way: each token keeps its own output vector"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "This is permutation equivariance."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "They all change to new vectors"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "Each token's output is unchanged. Only its place in the list moves."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "They stay in the same places, with the same vectors"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "The outputs move with the tokens."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "They are all set to zero"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "Nothing is zeroed."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "teaches": ["attention-blind", "toy-swap"],
      "covers": ["position-need"],
      "variants": [
        {
          "prompt": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "In the toy check, the tokens (1, 0), (0, 1), (1, 1) are put in the reverse order. What is true of the outputs?"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "options": [
            {
              "correct": true,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "They are the same three vectors, in the reverse order"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "reason": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "Each token got exactly the same output as before."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "correct": false,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "They are three new vectors"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "reason": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "They match the original outputs."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "correct": false,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "They are identical to each other"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "reason": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "The tokens differ, so their outputs differ."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "correct": false,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "There are no outputs"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "reason": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "Attention still produces one output per token."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Why isn't the embedding lookup enough to give the model word order?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "options": [
        {
          "correct": true,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "A token gets the same embedding wherever it appears, so the vector carries no information about its place"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "Position has to come from somewhere else."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "The lookup table has no row for repeated tokens"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "It has a row for every token in the vocabulary."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "The lookup returns vectors of different lengths"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "Every token vector has the same length, d_model."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "The lookup only works for the first token"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "It works for every token."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "teaches": ["embedding-no-place"],
      "covers": ["position-need"],
      "variants": [
        {
          "prompt": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "The token "
                },
                {
                  "text": "cat",
                  "italic": true
                },
                {
                  "text": " appears at position 2 and again at position 9. Straight after the embedding lookup, how do the two vectors compare?"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "options": [
            {
              "correct": true,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "They are identical"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "reason": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "A lookup depends only on the token, not on its place."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "correct": false,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "They differ, because the positions differ"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "reason": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "The lookup does not see the position."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "correct": false,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "They differ by the number of tokens in between"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "reason": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "Nothing like that is added by the lookup."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "correct": false,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "Only the first one exists"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "reason": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "Both positions get a vector."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Which of these is a way of solving the problem?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "options": [
        {
          "correct": true,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "Supply position information explicitly, so a token at one place is treated differently from the same token elsewhere"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "That is what the position schemes do."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "Sort the tokens alphabetically before attention"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "That would destroy the very order the model needs."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "Use a larger vocabulary"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "A bigger vocabulary does not tell the model where tokens are."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "Remove attention"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "Attention is what lets tokens exchange information. The problem is what it cannot see."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "teaches": ["the-fix", "nuance"],
      "covers": ["position-need"],
      "variants": [
